# Participant secrets for Basis protocol
#
# SECURITY: this file must NOT be committed. `secrets/participants.csv` is gitignored, and a copy
# that was previously committed held live mainnet-format keys -- those keys are public now and must
# be rotated before any deployment.
#
# Format: name,address,secret_hex
#
# Usage:
#   cp secrets/participants.csv.template secrets/participants.csv
#   # then fill in the rows below with your own keys
#
# The Scala reference implementation reads scala/secrets/participants.local.csv instead; see
# scala/secrets/participants.csv.template. The committed scala/secrets/participants.csv is a
# TEST FIXTURE with throwaway keys and is safe to commit.
#
# `basis_cli --demo` falls back to deterministic test-only keys when this file is absent, so a
# missing file degrades to a clearly-labelled demo mode rather than failing.
#
# Generate a keypair with:
#   python3 demo/demo_keygen.py
#
tracker,<tracker_p2pk_address>,<tracker_secret_hex>
alice,<alice_p2pk_address>,<alice_secret_hex>
bob,<bob_p2pk_address>,<bob_secret_hex>
